-- l4 lint fixture: the s 8(3) of the Probate Act says "Subject to section 6"
-- and its body never calls the decision for section 6. A finding.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons` n MEANS
    n GREATER THAN 4

@ref Probate Act s 8(3) — "Subject to section 6, probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed."
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) — probate may be granted` n MEANS
        "Subject to section 6,"
    ... n GREATER THAN 1
